{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["The reason for <b>So the children of Israel stripped themselves of their ornaments</b> (ובני ישראל התנצלו מעדים): when they heard this, they stripped themselves and removed every ornament, more than they had done at first. And Onkelos (Onkelos on Exodus 33:6), who translated \"ornaments\" (עדי) as \" weaponry\" (תקון זין) — his intent is like the words of the one who said in Bereshit Rabbah (see Shemot Rabbah 45b): \"weapons (זינאות) He girded upon them,\" that is, the Holy One, blessed be He, girded them at the time of the giving of the Torah with weapons to be saved from every plague and from the Angel of Death, as the Sages expounded (Shemot Rabbah 32a) on \"engraved on the tablets\" (חרות על הלוחות, Exodus 32:16) — freedom (חרות) from the Angel of Death — and these are the names of the Holy One, blessed be He. Now Israel accepted upon themselves death with willing soul because of the punishment for the calf, and this is the matter of great repentance and remorse for their sin."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The citation 'Bereshit Rabbah' likely refers to the passage in Shemot Rabbah as the cross-reference itself indicates; I have rendered the Aramaic 'זינאות' as 'weapons' and noted the Hebrew original in parentheses where it aids the argument."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:20.045694500Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}